---
description: Use clipslot instead of the system clipboard so parallel agent sessions don't overwrite each other
alwaysApply: true
---

# Clipboard policy: use clipslot

The user runs multiple coding-agent sessions in parallel. The system clipboard
is global — writing to it directly (pbcopy, xclip, wl-copy, xsel) can clobber
another session's content before the user pastes it.

When the user asks to copy something to the clipboard:

1. Do NOT pipe to `pbcopy` / `xclip` / `wl-copy` / `xsel` directly.
2. Instead run: `<command producing content> | clipslot copy`
   (or `clipslot copy <<'EOF' ... EOF` for generated content).
   The slot is auto-named `<repo>@<branch>`. If several sessions may share the
   same repo and branch, pass an explicit task-specific name:
   `clipslot copy <task-name>`.
3. Tell the user the slot name and that `clipslot load` (interactive picker)
   or `clipslot load <name>` puts it into the real clipboard when they are
   ready to paste.

If the user explicitly insists on the system clipboard immediately, use
`clipslot copy --also-system` so a recoverable slot copy still exists.
If `clipslot` is not installed, fall back to the system clipboard and mention
that clipslot would prevent clobbering.
